pal null congruence: the two null directions of the plane of $\\partial_q$ and $(q^2 + \\ell^2)\\,\\partial_\\tau - \\partial_\\sigma$, which are the repeated principal null directions of the Weyl tensor. Every ray turns as it goes, at $d\\sigma/dq = \\mp 1/Q$, and the curves drawn are the rays' projections, $d(c\\tau)/dq = \\pm(q^2 + \\ell^2)/Q$, the same at every $p$.","The rays are null geodesics, and each cone is the future cone of the principal plane. The cones close at $q_+ = \\ell$ and point to smaller $q$ inside it. The dotted line is the ergosurface, $Q = P$, at $q = 1.180\\,\\ell$ on the equator, and between it and $q_+$ nothing, light included, can keep $\\sigma$ fixed."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains","weyl_tensor","christoffel"],"version":"fc9f9c5601fd2340"}}]}}
